      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "No not anymore I fixed the Issue myself. It's pretty easy to fix actually but took some time to figure that out.\n\nGo to your FX-Layer from your Avatar.\n\nThen in your Animator go to the \"All\" layer and remove the Mask\n\nthat was inplemented there. While doing it the M on the left side should be gone. It should look like the screenshot below.\n\nAfter I have done it everything was working again how it was intendet.\n\nI hope this will help you guys also.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
